  "title": "RiskEngine.twapEMA() tuple destructuring mismatch ignores eonsEMA and includes spotEMA, breaking TWAP manipulation resistance used in liquidation checks",
  "severity": "high",
  "validity": "valid",
  "quality": "sufficient",
  "user_handle": "dtang",
  "body": "## Root Cause\n\n`RiskEngine.twapEMA()` ([RiskEngine.sol#L836-L840](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L836-L840)) destructures the return values of `OraclePack.getEMAs()` ([OraclePack.sol#L209-L214](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/types/OraclePack.sol#L209-L214)) in the wrong order.\n\n**`getEMAs()` returns:** `(spotEMA, fastEMA, slowEMA, eonsEMA, medianTick)`\n\n**`twapEMA()` destructures as:** `(eonsEMA, slowEMA, fastEMA, , )`\n\n| Position | `getEMAs()` Returns | Variable in `twapEMA()` | Actual Value | Weight |\n|----------|---------------------|-------------------------|--------------|--------|\n| 1st | `_spotEMA` | `eonsEMA` | **spotEMA** ❌ | 10% |\n| 2nd | `_fastEMA` | `slowEMA` | **fastEMA** ❌ | 30% |\n| 3rd | `_slowEMA` | `fastEMA` | **slowEMA** ❌ | 60% |\n| 4th | `_eonsEMA` | *(ignored)* | **discarded!** ❌ | 0% |\n\n**Intended formula:** `(6 * fastEMA + 3 * slowEMA + eonsEMA) / 10`\n\n**Actual formula:** `(6 * slowEMA + 3 * fastEMA + spotEMA) / 10`\n\nThe helper accessors in [OraclePack.sol#L169-L200](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/types/OraclePack.sol#L169-L200) confirm the correct return order.\n\n## Impact\n\nPer the NatSpec: *\"This heavily smoothed value is designed to be highly resistant to manipulation and serves as a robust price feed for critical system functions like solvency checks.\"*\n\n**However, the implementation computes a 60/30/10 blend of (slow, fast, spot) instead of (fast, slow, eons). `eonsEMA` has zero influence on the returned TWAP.**\n\nThis TWAP is used in `PanopticPool.getTWAP()` ([PanopticPool.sol#L1944-L1945](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1944-L1945)) which feeds into:\n- Liquidation solvency checks (`atTicks[1] = twapTick`) ([PanopticPool.sol#L1392-L1397](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1392-L1397))\n- `StaleOracle` gate: `|currentTick - twapTick| > tickDeltaLiquidation` ([PanopticPool.sol#L1378-L1389](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-12-panoptic/blob/main/contracts/PanopticPool.sol#L1378-L1389))\n- `_settlePremium()` and `_forceExercise()` pricing\n\nIf short-horizon price movement propagates into `spotEMA` faster than longer-horizon EMAs:\n1. The buggy TWAP incorporates that movement with 10% weight (should be 0%)\n2. This alters outcomes of the `StaleOracle` safety boundary and solvency evaluation\n3. System may proceed when it should revert as stale, or revert when it should proceed\n\n**Impacts liquidation correctness and liveness:**\n- Blocked liquidations → bad debt may accumulate\n- Incorrect liquidations → borderline solvent accounts may be flagged insolvent\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\n**Minimal fix:** Destructure `getEMAs()` in correct order, or use typed accessors to avoid tuple-footguns.\n\nfunction twapEMA(OraclePack oraclePack) external pure returns (int24) {\n    int256 fast = oraclePack.fastEMA();\n    int256 slow = oraclePack.slowEMA();\n    int256 eons = oraclePack.eonsEMA();\n    return int24((6 * fast + 3 * slow + eons) / 10);\n}",
  "proof_of_concept": "Place at `test/foundry/core/RiskEngine/TwapEMABugPoC.t.sol` and run:\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract TwapEMABugPoC -vvv\n```\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {RiskEngine} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {OraclePack, OraclePackLibrary} from \"@types/OraclePack.sol\";\n\ncontract TwapEMABugPoC is Test {\n    RiskEngine riskEngine;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        riskEngine = new RiskEngine(10000, 10000, address(0), address(0));\n    }\n\n    /// @notice SMOKING GUN: eonsEMA is completely ignored\n    function test_eonsEMA_is_completely_ignored() public {\n        uint96 pack1 = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(100, 100, 100, 100);\n        uint96 pack2 = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(100, 100, 100, 9999);\n        \n        OraclePack op1 = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, uint256(pack1), 0, 0, 0, 0);\n        OraclePack op2 = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, uint256(pack2), 0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        int24 r1 = riskEngine.twapEMA(op1);\n        int24 r2 = riskEngine.twapEMA(op2);\n\n        console.log(\"eonsEMA=100  -> twapEMA:\", r1);\n        console.log(\"eonsEMA=9999 -> twapEMA:\", r2);\n\n        // eonsEMA changed 100 -> 9999, but result is IDENTICAL\n        assertEq(r1, r2, \"BUG: eonsEMA is completely ignored!\");\n    }\n\n    /// @notice SMOKING GUN: spotEMA incorrectly affects output\n    function test_spotEMA_incorrectly_affects_output() public {\n        uint96 pack1 = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(100, 100, 100, 100);\n        uint96 pack2 = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(1000, 100, 100, 100);\n        \n        OraclePack op1 = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, uint256(pack1), 0, 0, 0, 0);\n        OraclePack op2 = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, uint256(pack2), 0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        int24 r1 = riskEngine.twapEMA(op1);\n        int24 r2 = riskEngine.twapEMA(op2);\n\n        console.log(\"spotEMA=100  -> twapEMA:\", r1);\n        console.log(\"spotEMA=1000 -> twapEMA:\", r2);\n        console.log(\"Delta (should be 0):\", r2 - r1);\n\n        // spotEMA changed, result DIFFERS (should NOT affect TWAP!)\n        assertTrue(r1 != r2, \"BUG: spotEMA affects twapEMA!\");\n        assertEq(r2 - r1, 90, \"spotEMA incorrectly has 10% weight\");\n    }\n\n    /// @notice Proves output matches buggy formula, not intended\n    function test_twapEMA_uses_wrong_values() public {\n        // spot=1000, fast=100, slow=200, eons=50\n        uint96 packed = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(1000, 100, 200, 50);\n        OraclePack op = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, uint256(packed), 0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        int24 result = riskEngine.twapEMA(op);\n\n        int24 intended = int24((6 * 100 + 3 * 200 + 50) / 10);  // = 125\n        int24 buggy = int24((6 * 200 + 3 * 100 + 1000) / 10);   // = 250\n\n        console.log(\"Intended (6*fast + 3*slow + eons)/10 =\", intended);\n        console.log(\"Buggy (6*slow + 3*fast + spot)/10 =\", buggy);\n        console.log(\"Actual from contract =\", result);\n\n        assertEq(result, buggy, \"Matches buggy formula\");\n        assertTrue(result != intended, \"Does NOT match intended formula\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Output (3/3 PASS)\n\n```\n[PASS] test_eonsEMA_is_completely_ignored()\n  eonsEMA=100  -> twapEMA: 100\n  eonsEMA=9999 -> twapEMA: 100\n\n[PASS] test_spotEMA_incorrectly_affects_output()\n  spotEMA=100  -> twapEMA: 100\n  spotEMA=1000 -> twapEMA: 190\n  Delta (should be 0): 90\n\n[PASS] test_twapEMA_uses_wrong_values()\n  Intended (6*fast + 3*slow + eons)/10 = 125\n  Buggy (6*slow + 3*fast + spot)/10 = 250\n  Actual from contract = 250\n```",
